code-review: install it as /code-rabbit-review, beside the built-in.

Upstream (coderabbitai/skills) names this skill `code-review`, the name
of Claude Code's own /code-review (the code-review plugin), and claims to
be the default for any review request. Installed under that name it
shadowed the built-in. Rename it in its frontmatter — tools/skills-update.sh
installs the directory as code-rabbit-review — and leave a plain review
request to the built-in.

Applied over the vendored copy by tools/skills-update.sh; git apply
skips this text before the first diff header.

diff --git a/.claude/skills/code-review/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/code-review/SKILL.md
index 219bc39..677a715 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/code-review/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/code-review/SKILL.md
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 ---
-name: code-review
-description: "Run CodeRabbit CLI reviews, retrieve saved local or GitHub PR fix prompts, and interpret CodeRabbit authentication and review output. Use for CodeRabbit review commands, committed/uncommitted or directory scopes, and CodeRabbit runbooks. Default code-review skill: also trigger for explicit code/PR/quality/security review requests or when a review is needed."
+name: code-rabbit-review
+description: "Run CodeRabbit CLI reviews, retrieve saved local or GitHub PR fix prompts, and interpret CodeRabbit authentication and review output. Use for CodeRabbit review commands, committed/uncommitted or directory scopes, and CodeRabbit runbooks. Invoke as /code-rabbit-review, or when CodeRabbit is named; a plain code review request is the built-in /code-review's."
